Notes:
	AlexAligned Unified v7, RealTest cross-check for the web terminal's Backtest section.
	This script does NOT reimplement the terminal's rotation logic. It trades a FIXED, externally
	supplied sequence of portfolio weights -- one row per (rebalance date, symbol held on that
	date) -- coming straight from the terminal's own "Download Terminal_Weights.csv" export in
	the Backtest tab. RealTest's job here is only to price that exact sequence of positions with
	its own fill/commission/slippage model and report the resulting equity curve, return, and
	drawdown, as an independent second engine checking the terminal's own numbers for the SAME
	portfolio and date range.

	BEFORE RUNNING:
	1. In the web terminal, open the Backtest section for the portfolio you want to check and use
	   its "Download Terminal_Weights.csv" export.
	2. Copy that file, unchanged, next to this script: C:\RealTest21_newerv2\Scripts\SectorTerminalScripts\Terminal_Weights.csv
	   (same folder this .rts file lives in -- the DataValueFile: line below finds it with
	   ?scriptpath?, so it does not matter which drive/folder that is, as long as the CSV sits
	   right next to the script).
	3. Confirm the StartDate/EndDate in TestSettings below actually cover the CSV's date range
	   (see the comment there) -- if the terminal's Backtest window has moved on since this file
	   was written, edit those two dates to match before running.
	4. Run Run_AlexAligned_v7_Validate_TerminalWeights.bat (or run_v7_Validate_TerminalWeights.ps1
	   directly). It calls RealTest.exe in Test mode (-test), never -import, so it never touches
	   the shared alexaligned_unified_v7.rtd data file -- it only reads it.

	HOW THE WEIGHTS DRIVE POSITION SIZE:
	Terminal_Weights.csv has header Date,Symbol,Weight (Weight a decimal fraction of portfolio
	value, e.g. 0.125). It is loaded with DataValueFile: below into a Data item named exactly
	"Weight" (RealTest's DataValueFile: matches by CSV column header = Data item name). A symbol
	still held on a later rebalance date gets a fresh row for that date too -- the CSV never
	relies on "no row = still held". That means: on a date where the CSV has ANY row at all (a
	rebalance date), a symbol with NO row that date is being told to exit; a symbol WITH a row is
	being told to hold exactly that target weight. On any other date (no rows at all -- not a
	rebalance date), nothing should change. RebalCount below (a #Count breadth check) tells the
	strategy's Quantity formula which of those three cases it is in, using the DynamicSizing
	rebalance idiom from the RealTest 2.1 script reference ("DynamicSizing for position
	adjustment" example): NaN = leave position alone, 0 = exit, positive = set target size.

	DATA REUSE: this script does NOT re-import anything. It reuses the shared .rtd file that
	part C's Import: block already builds (see AlexAligned_Unified_v7_C_EngineFree_25.09.2026.rts)
	via DataFile: below, exactly like part E does. Run part C with -import first if that file does
	not exist yet on this machine.

	FIX (this version): a first real run showed RealTest generating far more trades than the
	terminal's own backtest (~1,900 vs ~960) for the same portfolio/window, with the SAME symbol
	entered once but exited in several pieces on different dates ("reduce position" then "zero
	position"). This was traced to a real semantic mismatch, not a RealTest bug: the CSV recomputes
	and writes a FRESH weight for a held symbol on every date it's held (so "no row" unambiguously
	means "exit"), but the terminal's own engine() NEVER re-weights an existing holding -- weighting
	is applied only at the moment of a brand-new buy, and a position already held keeps its original
	size for its whole life. The old Quantity formula below treated every date's recomputed weight
	as a fresh resize command, so RealTest was correctly, faithfully doing what it was told: trimming
	the position a little every time the recomputed equal-weight fraction shifted (which happens
	whenever the basket size changes by one name) -- each trim becoming its own closed trade, exactly
	as RealTest's own partial-exit accounting is documented to do (ExitQty/ExitLimitQty/ExitStopQty
	are first-class concepts; a trade record can only carry one exit date/price). The fix is the
	`Shares <> 0` check added to Quantity below: a symbol already holding shares is left alone
	(NaN = no change) regardless of that date's recomputed weight, matching the terminal's real
	"weight fixed at purchase" semantics exactly. Only a symbol with zero shares (a genuine new
	entry) gets sized from the CSV's Weight.

	VALIDATED SYNTAX, STILL UNVALIDATED END-TO-END: `Shares` as a position variable readable in a
	DynamicSizing Quantity formula is documented in the RealTest 2.1 script language reference
	(STRATEGY ELEMENTS, position variables: "Shares -- current shares/contracts in position"). The
	rest of the script (DataValueFile:/DynamicSizing:/Select()) was confirmed against a real run
	already (the earlier "cannot specify Side" and successful runs). This specific change --
	Shares <> 0 skipping a resize -- has not itself been run yet; if RealTest reports any parse
	error, please report the exact text back before hand-editing around it.

Settings:
	DataFile:	C:\RealTest21_newerv2\Data\alexaligned_unified_v7.rtd
	BarSize:	Daily
	EndDate:	Latest
	AccountSize:	100000
	UseAvailableBars:	False
	SaveTradesAs:	?scriptpath?\AlexAligned_Unified_v7_Validate_TerminalWeights_Trades.csv
	SaveTestListAs:	?scriptpath?\AlexAligned_Unified_v7_Validate_TerminalWeights_Results.csv
	SaveStatsAs:	?scriptpath?\AlexAligned_Unified_v7_Validate_TerminalWeights_Equity.csv

	// StartDate lives in TestSettings only, matching the convention in parts C/E of this repo
	// (a StartDate directly in Settings has caused problems for those scripts' ScanSettings
	// interaction; this script has no ScanSettings section at all, but TestSettings is kept
	// here anyway for consistency and because it is the documented place to override dates
	// for Test-mode runs).
TestSettings:
	// CONFIRM these against the Terminal_Weights.csv you actually downloaded before running.
	// 2025-09-15 / 2026-09-25 is the last documented terminal Backtest window as of this
	// writing (docs/FINAL_HANDOFF_2026-09-28_0100UTC.txt, Part F: "Replayed 260
	// rebalance-eligible dates, 2025-09-15 to 2026-09-25"). If the portfolio you exported used
	// a different window, edit both lines below to match it -- a mismatched window will not
	// error, it will just silently compare the wrong stretch of the terminal's own numbers.
	StartDate:	2025-09-15
	EndDate:	2026-09-25

Data:
	// Loads Terminal_Weights.csv (header Date,Symbol,Weight) via DataValueFile:. The Data item
	// name below MUST be "Weight" -- DataValueFile: matches by CSV column header = Data item
	// name (RealTest 2.1 script reference, DataValueFile section). Rows for a date/symbol not
	// in the CSV leave Weight as NaN for that symbol on that date, exactly as documented.
	DataValueFile:	?scriptpath?\Terminal_Weights.csv
	Weight:	#DataValueFile

	// RebalCount = 0 on any date the CSV has no rows at all for ANY symbol (i.e. not one of the
	// terminal's rebalance dates); > 0 on an actual rebalance date. #Count expr counts symbols
	// where expr is not NaN (breadth operators section of the reference), so this is a genuine
	// cross-sectional check, not a per-symbol one -- every symbol sees the same RebalCount value
	// on a given date.
	RebalCount:	#Count Weight

Strategy: TerminalWeights
	// No Side: line -- RealTest rejects "Side" on a DynamicSizing strategy (confirmed by a real
	// run: "Dynamic-sizing strategy TerminalWeights cannot specify Side"). Side is implied by the
	// SIGN of Quantity instead (RealTest 2.1 reference, DynamicSizing section: positive = long,
	// negative = short) -- our Quantity below is always positive (Weight * 100, Weight a 0-1
	// fraction from Terminal_Weights.csv), so this strategy is long-only exactly as before,
	// just without the now-illegal explicit Side: line.
	// Generous headroom above whatever BasketN/MBPositions the terminal used -- DynamicSizing
	// positions are still capped by MaxPositions, so raise this if RealTest ever reports it
	// could not open all the CSV's held names on some date.
	MaxPositions:	60
	QtyType:	Percent
	DynamicSizing:	True
	// NaN = no change, 0 = exit, positive = set position to that target weight. In order:
	//   RebalCount = 0   -> not a rebalance date at all -> NaN (no change)
	//   IsNaN(Weight)    -> rebalance date, symbol absent from the CSV -> 0 (exit)
	//   Shares <> 0      -> rebalance date, symbol present, ALREADY HELD -> NaN (no change --
	//                       matches the terminal's own engine(), which never re-weights an
	//                       existing holding; only a brand-new buy gets sized)
	//   else             -> rebalance date, symbol present, NOT currently held -> a genuine new
	//                       entry -> Weight * 100 (Weight is a 0-1 fraction in the CSV; QtyType:
	//                       Percent wants 0-100, hence * 100)
	Quantity:	Select(RebalCount = 0, nan, IsNaN(Weight), 0, Shares <> 0, nan, Weight * 100)
	// Minimum position value if DynamicSizing needs to shrink a target weight to fit inside
	// MaxExposure/MaxPositions -- see the DynamicSizing example in the RealTest 2.1 reference.
	Reduce:	0.01 * S.Alloc

	// No documented Commission:/Slippage: convention to copy from
	// AlexAligned_Unified_v7_C_EngineFree_25.09.2026.rts -- that script is Import/Scan only and
	// has no Strategy section at all, so there is nothing to match for "a fair comparison" as
	// instructed. These two lines are instead the reference doc's own worked example values
	// (STRATEGY EXAMPLES, Example 3's Template: common block), a reasonable generic assumption
	// for a US equity account -- $1 minimum or 0.5% of trade value commission, 0.2% of fill
	// price slippage. Edit both to 0 if you want a zero-friction comparison against the
	// terminal's own numbers (the terminal's Backtest section may not model costs at all).
	Commission:	Max(1, 0.005 * Shares)
	Slippage:	0.002 * FillPrice

Graphs:
	// Required for SaveStatsAs to produce anything (reference doc, CSV OUTPUT SETTINGS section).
	Equity:	Combined(S.Equity)
